To configure the reverse proxy, update the Nginx configuration file located at /etc/nginx/nginx.conf. Add the following block inside the http context:

```
upstream backend {
    server 127.0.0.1:8080;
    keepalive 64;
}

server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name api.example.com;
    location / {
        proxy_pass http://backend;
        proxy_set_header Connection "";
    }
}
```

After modifying the configuration, run `nginx -t` to validate the syntax, then execute `systemctl reload nginx` to apply the changes without dropping existing connections. Ensure that the SSL certificate at /etc/ssl/certs/api.example.com.crt is valid and has not expired.

